---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Game Modes in 16-0 Play | Classic, Franchise, Gamble, Multiplayer"
  description="Compare Classic, Franchise, Gamble, and Multiplayer in 16-0 Play. Learn how squads, auctions, ratings, and season results work."
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://16-0play.com/game-modes/" />
    <meta property="og:title" content="Game Modes in 16-0 Play" />
    <meta property="og:description" content="Compare the four ways to play 16-0 Play and learn how team strength and season results work." />
  </Fragment>

  <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-6xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 md:py-16">
    <header class="mb-12 max-w-3xl">
      <h1 class="mb-5 text-4xl font-black tracking-tight text-[var(--color-ink)] sm:text-5xl">Choose how you want to play</h1>
      <p class="max-w-2xl text-lg leading-8 text-[var(--color-body)]">Build a cricket squad, guide it through a season, or bid for players with friends.</p>
    </header>

    <section aria-labelledby="mode-options">
      <h2 id="mode-options" class="mb-6 text-2xl font-bold text-[var(--color-ink)] sm:text-3xl">Four ways to take on the challenge</h2>
      <div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
        <article class="rounded-xl border border-[var(--color-hairline)] bg-[var(--color-canvas-soft)] p-6 sm:p-7">
          <h3 class="mb-3 text-xl font-bold text-[var(--color-ink)]">Classic</h3>
          <p class="mb-5 leading-7 text-[var(--color-body)]">Pick an all-time team of Indian Premier League (IPL) players and play a full simulated season. This is the most direct way to learn player roles, team strength, and the race for the playoffs.</p>
          <dl class="grid gap-3 border-t border-[var(--color-hairline)] pt-4 text-sm sm:grid-cols-2">
            <div><dt class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]">Starting team</dt><dd class="mt-1 text-[var(--color-mute)]">11 players</dd></div>
            <div><dt class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]">Overseas limit</dt><dd class="mt-1 text-[var(--color-mute)]">Up to 4 in the starting eleven</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </article>

        <article class="rounded-xl border border-[var(--color-hairline)] bg-[var(--color-canvas-soft)] p-6 sm:p-7">
          <h3 class="mb-3 text-xl font-bold text-[var(--color-ink)]">Franchise</h3>
          <p class="mb-5 leading-7 text-[var(--color-body)]">Manage a deeper squad and prepare for each match. Keep reserves for flexibility, then choose the eleven starters and impact bench before the game.</p>
          <dl class="grid gap-3 border-t border-[var(--color-hairline)] pt-4 text-sm sm:grid-cols-2">
            <div><dt class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]">Squad size</dt><dd class="mt-1 text-[var(--color-mute)]">Up to 25 players</dd></div>
            <div><dt class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]">Overseas players</dt><dd class="mt-1 text-[var(--color-mute)]">Up to 8 in the squad, 4 in the starting eleven</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </article>

        <article class="rounded-xl border border-[var(--color-hairline)] bg-[var(--color-canvas-soft)] p-6 sm:p-7">
          <h3 class="mb-3 text-xl font-bold text-[var(--color-ink)]">Gamble</h3>
          <p class="mb-5 leading-7 text-[var(--color-body)]">The game builds a squad around a randomly chosen team philosophy. Review the players and their strengths, then decide whether you want to continue with that team. No wagering is involved.</p>
          <dl class="grid gap-3 border-t border-[var(--color-hairline)] pt-4 text-sm sm:grid-cols-2">
            <div><dt class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]">Squad selection</dt><dd class="mt-1 text-[var(--color-mute)]">Generated for you</dd></div>
            <div><dt class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]">Your choice</dt><dd class="mt-1 text-[var(--color-mute)]">Continue or try another team</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </article>

        <article class="rounded-xl border border-[var(--color-hairline)] bg-[var(--color-canvas-soft)] p-6 sm:p-7">
          <h3 class="mb-3 text-xl font-bold text-[var(--color-ink)]">Multiplayer</h3>
          <p class="mb-5 leading-7 text-[var(--color-body)]">Create a room or join with its code, then build teams through a timed auction. Watch the bids and your purse as you compete with other people and AI teams for players.</p>
          <dl class="grid gap-3 border-t border-[var(--color-hairline)] pt-4 text-sm sm:grid-cols-2">
            <div><dt class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]">Room size</dt><dd class="mt-1 text-[var(--color-mute)]">Up to 10 teams</dd></div>
            <div><dt class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]">Host settings</dt><dd class="mt-1 text-[var(--color-mute)]">Roster, timer, overseas limit, and auction pool</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="team-strength" class="mt-16 border-t border-[var(--color-hairline)] pt-12">
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <h2 id="team-strength" class="mb-4 text-2xl font-bold text-[var(--color-ink)] sm:text-3xl">What affects team strength?</h2>
        <p class="mb-6 leading-7 text-[var(--color-body)]">The rating on a player profile is only one part of your starting eleven. The game weighs each player's rating by role, then adjusts the team's values for lineup choices. Use the breakdown on the lineup screen to see how your selections fit together.</p>
        <ul class="space-y-4 text-[var(--color-body)]">
          <li><strong class="text-[var(--color-ink)]">Roles:</strong> Batters and wicketkeepers contribute to batting strength; specialist bowlers contribute to bowling strength. All-rounders help with both.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-[var(--color-ink)]">Chemistry and rivalries:</strong> Some listed player pairs add chemistry points, while some pairings create a deduction. The <a class="font-medium underline underline-offset-4" href="/guides/signature-pairs/">signature-pairs guide</a> has the full list.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-[var(--color-ink)]">Rating stacking:</strong> The first two players rated 92 or above avoid the 92-plus deduction. Additional high-rated players can lose some effective rating, with another deduction for later 95-plus players.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-[var(--color-ink)]">Overseas players:</strong> A standard starting eleven can have up to four. Two overseas players lower overall by one point, three by two, and four by three. Multiplayer rooms may set a different limit.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-[var(--color-ink)]">Team identity:</strong> Certain role mixes and groups of players from the same former franchise can add points. These bonuses help refine a lineup; they do not replace role coverage.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-6 leading-7 text-[var(--color-body)]">A team overall above 90 has diminishing returns: half of the amount above 90 is removed. That is not a hard cap. The <a class="font-medium underline underline-offset-4" href="/rating-system/">rating-system guide</a> explains these rules with examples.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="season-results" class="mt-16 border-t border-[var(--color-hairline)] pt-12">
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <h2 id="season-results" class="mb-4 text-2xl font-bold text-[var(--color-ink)] sm:text-3xl">Season length and match results</h2>
        <p class="mb-4 leading-7 text-[var(--color-body)]">A standard season has ten teams divided into two groups. Each team plays 14 regular-season matches. The top four move on to Qualifier 1, the Eliminator, Qualifier 2, and the Final. The “16-0” name is the challenge goal, not the number of regular-season matches.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 leading-7 text-[var(--color-body)]">A win gives a team two points. If rain abandons a regular-season match, both teams receive one point and the match is counted as neither a win nor a loss. Rain can also shorten a match and label its result. The game does not use the official Duckworth–Lewis–Stern method that sets targets in real cricket. Read <a class="font-medium underline underline-offset-4" href="/guides/dls-rain-events/">the rain and reduced-overs guide</a> for details.</p>
        <p class="leading-7 text-[var(--color-body)]">Calculated team strength helps shape the chance of winning, but it cannot guarantee a result. Form, match events, and randomness can still produce an upset.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="mode-questions" class="mt-16 border-t border-[var(--color-hairline)] pt-12">
      <h2 id="mode-questions" class="mb-6 text-2xl font-bold text-[var(--color-ink)] sm:text-3xl">Common questions</h2>
      <div class="max-w-3xl divide-y divide-[var(--color-hairline)]">
        <details class="group py-4">
          <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)] focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 focus-visible:outline-yellow-500">Which mode should I try first?</summary>
          <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-[var(--color-body)]">Start with Classic if you want to choose every player and learn how team strength works. Choose Franchise for a larger squad, Gamble for a team selected for you, or Multiplayer to bid with others.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="group py-4">
          <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)] focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 focus-visible:outline-yellow-500">Does Gamble use real money?</summary>
          <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-[var(--color-body)]">No. Gamble is the name of a game mode that generates a team around a random philosophy. It does not ask you to place bets or wager money.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="group py-4">
          <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)] focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 focus-visible:outline-yellow-500">Does the game use the official rain calculation?</summary>
          <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-[var(--color-body)]">No. The game can shorten a match and label its result, but it does not calculate targets with the full official Duckworth–Lewis–Stern method.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-16 rounded-xl border border-[var(--color-hairline)] bg-[var(--color-canvas-soft)] p-6 sm:p-8">
      <h2 class="mb-3 text-2xl font-bold text-[var(--color-ink)]">Ready to build a team?</h2>
      <p class="mb-5 max-w-2xl leading-7 text-[var(--color-body)]">Start a season, compare your lineup, and see how your choices hold up across the matches.</p>
      <a href="/" class="inline-flex min-h-11 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-yellow-500 px-5 py-3 font-bold text-black transition-colors hover:bg-yellow-400 focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-yellow-500">Play 16-0 Play</a>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
